selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.stagnation_pressure\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.stagnation_pressure\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stagnation_pressure</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Total pressure at each azimuthal station [Pa].</p><p>Aungier\u2019s analysis is lumped: it charges one coefficient per mechanism\nbetween the inlet and the collection plane, and says nothing about\nwhere round the volute each is spent. Spreading them linearly with\nazimuth is an assumption made so the passage can be coloured by\npressure, not a result of the model. It is a defensible one \u2013 the dump\nterms are paid as flow is collected, and collected flow grows linearly\nwith azimuth, while the friction term accumulates along a path length\nthat also grows with azimuth \u2013 but the endpoints are what the model\nactually pins down.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire-ducts-volute-voluteresult\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pyskyfire-ducts-volute-voluteresult\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.loss_breakdown\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.loss_breakdown\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">loss_breakdown</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">dict</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Loss coefficients by mechanism, for reporting.</p><p>The three exit terms are disjoint. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_cone</span></code> is the area change\ninto the flange, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_friction</span></code> the wall shear along the duct, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_bend</span></code> the cost of turning it. Where the cone tapers either\nway, the first two are the two halves of one Rennels coefficient \u2013\nevaluated at the real friction factor and at zero \u2013 rather than two\ncorrelations that might overlap.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.collection_loss\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.collection_loss\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">collection_loss</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Total pressure lost between the inlet and the collection plane [Pa].</p><p>Everything except the exit cone\u2019s three terms, which are spent in the\nduct downstream of it.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.volute.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">VoluteResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Loss breakdown and station conditions for one volute operating point.</p><p>All loss coefficients are referred to the inlet velocity head, so a total\npressure loss follows as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">omega</span> <span class=\"pre\">*</span> <span class=\"pre\">rho</span> <span class=\"pre\">*</span> <span class=\"pre\">C5**2</span> <span class=\"pre\">/</span> <span class=\"pre\">2</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.static_pressure\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.static_pressure\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">static_pressure</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Static pressure at each azimuthal station [Pa].</p><p>The local velocity head taken off the stagnation pressure above, so it\ninherits the same caveat. It starts at the inlet stagnation pressure,\nwhere nothing has been collected and the passage is still.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.collected_velocity\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.collected_velocity\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">collected_velocity</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Through-flow velocity at each azimuthal station [m/s].</p><p>Only the fraction <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">theta</span> <span class=\"pre\">/</span> <span class=\"pre\">(2*pi)</span></code> of the mass flow has been gathered\nby azimuth <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">theta</span></code>, so this is what the passage area at that station\nactually has to carry. It ends at <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">C_6</span></code>.</p><p>Under conservation of angular momentum it is the <em>product</em> with the\ncentroid radius that stays constant, not the velocity: the flow slows\nas the passage carries it outward. A constant-velocity law would be the\none holding this uniform.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.total_pressure_loss\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.total_pressure_loss\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">total_pressure_loss</span></span><span class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></dt><dd><p>Alias matching <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.exit_cone_pressures\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.volute.VoluteResult.exit_cone_pressures\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_cone_pressures</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">9</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Stagnation and static pressure along the exit cone [Pa].</p><p>Unlike the volute passage, the duct\u2019s losses really are spent between\ntwo stations the model pins down, so the stagnation pressure ramps\nlinearly between them rather than apportioning a lumped total. The\nvelocity is eased from <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">C_6</span></code> to <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">C_7</span></code> on the same smoothstep the\nswept duct\u2019s section morphs along, so the static pressure follows the\nrendered shape; only its endpoints carry model weight.</p><p>Returns <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(stagnation,</span> <span class=\"pre\">static)</span></code>, each with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></code> values, the\nfirst at the collection plane and the last at the flange.</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
